he new step is to filter noise first: 8-objects without couplers and isolated 9-clusters with unmatched sizes are static decoys and should be ignored.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b7bacbf/D2/1/code.py:74:#     - cavity filtering by len(boundary_colors)==1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D2/2/code.py:84:# - Full-width horizontal bars preserve the original striped look.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D8/0/code.py:55:#       only horizontal bar recognition changes; particle motion, blockers, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D8/0/code.py:88:#       variant focused on fragmented horizontal bars instead of adding extra\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D8/0/code.py:163:    \"\"\"Move particles through real corridors, allowing 1-cell gaps in horizontal bar pairs.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/26/code.py:68:#    the tight crop easy to read. Two-legend outputs are additionally filtered\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/0/code.py:73:#     - Original destination filtering assumed exactly one moving axis:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/0/code.py:78:- Entrance detection and the \"start only from genuine real corridors\" filter still\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b7bacbf/D4/0/code.py:30:#   seeds. Its old `if r == 0 ...` filter is invalid under the variant and must\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/3/code.py:20:#    direction, so it can be reused after candidate groups are filtered by region-color compatibility.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/3/code.py:74:    - A train first filters target stations by coupler count, so repeated station sizes produce a candidate set instead of a single hit.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/3/code.py:91:    # - filter candidate stations by COUPLER COUNT\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:44:#   solver-compatible. Additional validation only filters generated inputs; it\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/3/code.py:107:    \"\"\"Original entrance filter: first real horizontal corridor starting at col <= 3.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D10/0/code.py:45:#   UD\" rule. The source motif is filtered to be asymmetric under LR, UD, 180, and rot90, and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D4/2/code.py:24:#    horizontal bars on even rows, real corridors where opposite bars share a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/3/code.py:43:#    - `best_dest` filtering by collinearity (`tr0 == 0` or `tc0 == 0`) no longer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D13/2/code.py:42:# - The original \"unique offset\" check remains valid, but only after filtering\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:210:_BAR_START_OPTIONS = [2, 3]                 # leftmost column of horizontal bars\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/3/code.py:199:_BAR_START_OPTIONS = [2, 3]                 # leftmost column of horizontal bars\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/10/code.py:388:# more evenly after geometric feasibility filtering.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D13/0/code.py:52:#       solver therefore filters for a monochrome component whose bbox has a full\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D1/1/code.py:33:#    incorrectly self-match unless non-destinations are filtered out. The new solver builds\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D11/1/code.py:36:# - In the original solver, destination candidates were filtered by `d[\"shape\"] == head_shape`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D2/2/code.py:42:#    - Candidate corner gaps are filtered so each beam has at least a short unobstructed diagonal runway.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D1/4/code.py:62:      - Candidate positions are filtered by visible area class induced by clipping.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8e5c0c38/D3/2/code.py:508:        alt_filtered = [opt for opt in pool if opt[1] == min(x[1] for x in pool)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8e5c0c38/D3/2/code.py:509:        _, _, _, cell, color = random.choice(alt_filtered)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D12/0/code.py:90:# lookup. The generator guarantees this by filtering every distractor candidate against\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D4/0/code.py:31:# - The visual change is strong enough to notice because the instruction strip may move from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D4/0/code.py:170:    Key insight: the transformation logic for each marker color is unchanged; the only new challenge is that the instruction strip must be found on the grid edge before the original fill rule can be applied.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D9/3/code.py:107:    - Matching therefore cannot rely on area pre-filtering and must compare\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/3/code.py:59:#     - Original head-seed filtering excluded only bg/border/grey/orange. With blue inside the border, those\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D12/1/code.py:30:#      difference: matching no longer requires filtering distractor shapes or counting colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D12/1/code.py:194:    - The outside objects are a clean dictionary: shape identifies which hole family to fill, and color is read directly because there are no distractors or competing colors to filter out.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/12/code.py:407:# back to the easier one-legend branch after rejection filtering.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D6/1/code.py:32:#      The new behavior therefore changes the filtering stage, not the plus detector itself.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D16/1/code.py:656:        assert preferred, \"expected at least one direction after filtering\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/25/code.py:20:#   - Remove the `sep-2` filter. After sliding, every enclosed bg hole emits on all rows it spans.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D3/0/code.py:40:#     - The generator filters out samples with no frame-colored trail pixels, preventing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:38:   - Source placement is filtered so each source has exactly one destination in its encoded direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:62:     direction cone. Guarantee: generator filters source placements with the same direction test\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D9/0/code.py:315:BASE_GAP_RANGE = (1, 4)         # candidate starting gaps 1..3 (filtered per n_frames)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/31/code.py:11:#    - D5/2 then further filters the remaining background-colored cavities by area: after the color check, only background-filled trigger-side\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/31/code.py:20:#      This prevents the generator from collapsing back to the original rule and makes both new filters visually testable from a few examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D3/2/code.py:71:#     - generator biases toward denser, multi-gap layouts but still filters with the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/8/code.py:24:#   instead of either solid horizontal bars (seed) or solid diagonal fans (pure D2).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D4/0/code.py:43:#    - Distractors remain isolated singletons in a dedicated color and are filtered out by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D4/1/code.py:34:#    cases. Generator-side filtering additionally forces every frame to have at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D4/1/code.py:51:#    filters gap combinations so each chosen beam path is clear in the input grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/17/code.py:49:#   - The blocker sits one row higher than the blocked emitter, so its horizontal bar never overlaps the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D14/1/code.py:224:    - Endpoint sprites are filtered by the success of a border-color lookup: matching ones survive with transferred centers, and unmatched ones vanish like other discarded sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D6/1/code.py:29:#       to discard with an area>1 filter and easy for humans to spot as noise.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D6/2/code.py:47:#       pixels. Color-only filtering is now invalid; the solver must distinguish\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D1/1/code.py:15:#   The difference is that the sprite no longer filters candidates by its current\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D15/2/code.py:32:      filtering rule affects actual solver behavior rather than only the input distribution.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D15/2/code.py:219:    - The new work is not in beam physics but in object filtering: identify which frame candidates are actual sources before\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D14/0/code.py:68:      same-shape unit pieces would be swappable. The new solver first filters by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D8/0/code.py:28:#      This keeps the core rule focused on anomaly filtering instead of adding\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D11/0/code.py:53:#       2x2, 2x3, and 3x2 L-pairs. The generator keeps the same bbox validity filter.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/4/code.py:39:#      This prevents collapse to the base task or to the D6-only single-filter variant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/4/code.py:215:    Key insight: The hole still nominates candidate emitter rows, but two visible row filters sit beside it: the separator must open on that row and the dedicated marker lane must also flag that row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D11/1/code.py:17:#   locally, so the solver must filter them out by checking the legend rather than by shape alone.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D11/1/code.py:136:    Key insight: shape alone is insufficient in this variant because several extra L-pairs are decoys; the decisive filter is whether the color is listed in the legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D13/1/code.py:102:    # This filters out arbitrary background on the frame perimeter when the frame touches the grid edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D10/1/code.py:163:      a candidate filter before validating shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/36/code.py:37:#      space rather than inside another sprite. That keeps horizontal bars non-overlapping with black\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D3/0/code.py:337:    Key insight: the triangle still gives direction, but the decisive filter is the visible red-blue-green cycle, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f215267/D4/2/code.py:85:  - the only added inference is shape-based filtering (single-pixel vs multi-pixel)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/23/code.py:18:# - D6/1 keeps only the rows whose separator cell is a bg gap. That is the first filter.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/23/code.py:37:#   2. at least one blocked candidate row, so D6/1 actually filters something;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D9/1/code.py:80:# - Every marker strip is periodic with primitive travel-axis period 2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D9/1/code.py:251:    Continue marker strips away from '+' anchors by repeating their primitive tile to the boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D9/1/code.py:256:    - Each anchor has one attached marker strip; most strips are only a compact seed, while one strip is already shown as a short periodic prefix that stops before the border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/12/code.py:50:#    - Hole filtering originally rejected bg components touching rows `0/h-1` or columns\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D4/1/code.py:11:#    - Variant: keep the same vertex detection, edge filtering, start-vertex choice, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f215267/D6/2/code.py:21:#       Difference: color match is no longer sufficient; size filtering is required.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D12/0/code.py:20:  up and right, which is ambiguous. In the variant, the right marker is filtered\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D12/0/code.py:305:        f\"{dirs_with_candidates}, expected exactly one after obstacle filtering\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D12/0/code.py:381:    - After obstacle filtering, exactly one cardinal direction can contain reachable markers; move to the nearest one on that half-line and rotate to face that direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D5/2/code.py:25:#    horizontal bar centered on the slot anchor; a 7x3 vertical rectangle becomes a 3x7\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D5/2/code.py:30:#    along the base row become [3, 5, 7], producing horizontal bars in those three slots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D5/2/code.py:38:#    new horizontal bars while keeping the original left-to-right slot identity intact.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D4/3/code.py:45:#      still computed only as a recognition filter; rendering uses the vertex set.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f215267/D10/0/code.py:68:  - For repeated-color sprites, candidate positions are filtered so the intended\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dbff022c/D5/0/code.py:54:#   between palette and sprites. Filled sprites are additionally filtered so at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D4/0/code.py:266:      longer a filter on legal directions; the decisive cue is which aligned marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/3/code.py:31:#      and move the corner blocks into bar slots. The variant must first filter:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/3/code.py:39:#      dif